  "narrative": {
    "northStar": "Editorial phone companion",
    "overview": "Shield translates the user's America.gov reference into a simple native iPhone companion: pale neutral ground, white reading groups, deep navy actions, serif content headings and familiar sans controls. The reference supplies composure and the relationship between display and interface text. SwiftUI supplies the navigation, controls and adaptive text; no licensed reference font, photograph or website-scale composition is copied.\n\nAn 80-year-old's comprehension is the design bar. Plain labels, generous controls and one clear next action carry the work. Daily calls and messages remain within four familiar tabs. Setup, sharing, privacy and uncertain results retain the information needed for explicit choices. The decorative vocabulary stays sparse so the words can grow.",
    "keyCharacteristics": [
      "Pale neutral ground and white grouped reading surfaces, with navy ground and pale actions in Dark Mode.",
      "Native serif purpose and section headings; native sans body, controls, toolbars and navigation.",
      "Native tabs, lists, forms, switches, sheets, alerts and state feedback.",
      "Semantic Dynamic Type, wrapping text, content-based stacking and generous app-owned actions.",
      "Call outcomes, person context, sharing scope and sample-only state expressed in words as well as color.",
      "Flat surfaces, restrained SF Symbols and explicit choices with retained state and visible recovery."
    ],
    "rules": [
      {
        "name": "The Outcome Truth Rule",
        "body": "Pair outcome color with plain words or a familiar symbol; a checked, offered or answered call never implies an authenticated caller.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
